--   Description
----------------
--   This test ensures that the GEM Next Page functionality works properly.

-- Detailed Test Description
--
-- ********************************************************************************************* --
-- GEM has to exchange 6 next pages while the Link Partner 6 next pages to exchange.
-- ********************************************************************************************* --
--
-- 1.  Initialise the GEM for Gigabit Operation with PCS enabled. Furthermore, Auto-Negotiation is 
--     enabled.
-- 2.  Once the GEM enters AN_ENABLE state, it should start transmitting alternating /C/ codes with 
--     the Config_Reg field all zeros.
-- 3.  After the link timer in the GEM finishes counting, the GEM should then transmit alternating /C/
--     codes with the Conf_Reg field incdicating the same values that are in the PCS auto-negotiation 
--     advertisement register.  Bit 15 in the auto-negotiation advertisment register will be set to allow the 
--     exchange of next pages between the GEM and the link partner. (Enter into ABILITY_DETECT state)
-- 4.  Provide a link of /C/ codes corresponding to the abilities of the link partner (Bits 6(HD) and 5(FD) set
--     high in the Conf_Reg. and bit 15 (NP)).  The link partner must have the next page bit set
--     when it transmits its base page abilities in order to allow the exchange next page information
--     with the GEM. 
-- 5.  The GEM should then transmit alternating /C/ codes with the Conf_Reg field indicating the 
--     same values that are in the PCS auto-negotiation advertisement register plus bit 14 should be set high.
--     This bit tells the link partner that the GEM has successfully received the link partner's base
--     page information. (Enter into ACKNOWLEDGE_DETECT state)
-- 6.  Provide a link of /C/ codes which correspond to the link partner sending the contents of
--     its Auto-Neg. Advertisment register.  Furthermore, bit 14 will be set to indicate that
--     the link partner has successfully received the GEM's acknowledge. (Enter into COMPLETE_ACK.
--     state) 
-- 7.  Once the GEM enters COMPLETE_ACKNOWLEGE state, the GEM will trigger the PCS next page request interrupt.
--     Then, load the PCS auto-nego. next page register with the desired value. Bit 15 should be set
--     in the PCS Auto-Neg. Next Page register to tell the link partner it has next pages to exchange.
-- 8.  The GEM should transmit the contents of the PCS Auto-Negotiation Next Page Register. 
--     Note that the Link Partner has its NP bit set in it's base page advertisment register
--     to allow the exchange of Next Pages with the GEM. (Enter NEXT_PAGE_WAIT state)
--     (Message Page Field equals 0x7ff)
-- 9.  Provide a link of /C/ codes which correspond to the link partner sending a Message Page. 
--     (Enter ACKNOWLEDGE_DETECT state)
--     (Message Page Field equals 0x7ff)
-- 10. The GEM should then transmit alternating /C/ codes with the Conf_Reg field indicating the 
--     same values that are in the PCS next page register plus bit 14 should be set high.
--     This bit tells the link partner that the GEM has successfully received the link next
--     page information. 
--     (Message Page Field equals 0x7ff)
-- 11. Provide a link of /C/ codes which correspond to the link partner sending a Message Page. 
--     The link partner acknowledges the reception of the GEMs Next Page information. 
--     (Enter COMPLETE_ACKNOWLEDGE state)
--     (Message Page Field equals 0x7ff)
-- 12. Once the GEM enters COMPLETE_ACKNOWLEGE state, the GEM will trigger the PCS next page request interrupt.
--     Then, load the PCS auto-nego. next page register with the desired value. Bit 15 should be set
--     in the PCS Auto-Neg. Next Page register to tell the link partner it has next pages to exchange.
--     Contents of PCS Auto. Neg Next Page  Register
-- 13. The GEM should transmit the contents of the PCS Auto-Negotiation Next Page Register. 
--     Note that the Link Partner has its NP bit set in it's base page advertisment register
--     to allow the exchange of Next Pages with the GEM. (Enter NEXT_PAGE_WAIT state)
--     (Message Page Field equals 0x2aa)
-- 14. Provide a link of /C/ codes which correspond to the link partner sending a Message Page. 
--     Link partner does have Next Pages to exchange. (Enter ACKNOWLEDGE_DETECT state)
--     Contents of RX_CONFIG Register = PCS Auto. Neg Link Partner Next Page  Register
--     (Message Page Field equals 0x2aa)
-- 15. The GEM should then transmit alternating /C/ codes with the Conf_Reg field incdicating the 
--     same values that are in the PCS next page register plus bit 14 should be set high.
--     This bit tells the link partner that the GEM has successfully received the link next
--     page information. 
--     (Message Page Field equals 0x2aa)
-- 16. Provide a link of /C/ codes which correspond to the link partner sending a Message Page. 
--     Link partner does have Next Pages to exchange. Furthermore, the link partner
--     acknowledges the reception of the GEMs Next Page information. (Enter COMPLETE_ACKNOWLEDGE)
--     (Message Page Field equals 0x2aa)
-- 17. Once the GEM enters COMPLETE_ACKNOWLEGE state, the GEM will trigger the PCS next page request interrupt.
--     Then, load the PCS auto-nego. next page register with the desired value. Bit 15 should be set
--     in the PCS Auto-Neg. Next Page register to tell the link partner it has next pages to exchange.
--     Contents of PCS Auto. Neg Next Page  Register
-- 18. The GEM should transmit the contents of the PCS Auto-Negotiation Next Page Register. 
--     Note that the Link Partner has its NP bit set in it's base page advertisment register
--     to allow the exchange of Next Pages with the GEM. (Enter NEXT_PAGE_WAIT state)
--     (Message Page Field equals 0x000)
-- 19. Provide a link of /C/ codes which correspond to the link partner sending a Message Page. 
--     (Enter ACKNOWLEDGE_DETECT state)
--     (Message Page Field equals 0x000)
-- 20. The GEM should then transmit alternating /C/ codes with the Conf_Reg field incdicating the 
--     same values that are in the PCS next page register plus bit 14 should be set high.
--     This bit tells the link partner that the GEM has successfully received the link partner next
--     page information. 
--     (Message Page Field equals 0x000)
-- 21. Provide a link of /C/ codes which correspond to the link partner sending a Message Page. 
--     The link partner acknowledges the reception of the GEMs Next Page information. 
--     (Enter COMPLETE_ACKNOWLEDGE state)
--     (Message Page Field equals 0x000)
-- 22. Once the GEM enters COMPLETE_ACKNOWLEGE state, the GEM will trigger the PCS next page request interrupt.
--     Then, load the PCS auto-nego. next page register with the desired value. Bit 15 should be set
--     in the PCS Auto-Neg. Next Page register to tell the link partner it has next pages to exchange.
--     Contents of PCS Auto. Neg Next Page  Register
-- 23. The GEM should transmit the contents of the PCS Auto-Negotiation Next Page Register. 
--     Note that the Link Partner has its NP bit set in it's base page advertisment register
--     to allow the exchange of Next Pages with the GEM. (Enter NEXT_PAGE_WAIT state)
--     Contents of TX_CONFIG Register = PCS Auto. Neg Next Page  Register
--     (Message Page Field equals 0x555)
-- 24. Provide a link of /C/ codes which correspond to the link partner sending a Message Page. 
--     Link partner does have Next Pages to exchange. (Enter ACKNOWLEDGE_DETECT state)
--     Contents of RX_CONFIG Register = PCS Auto. Neg Link Partner Next Page  Register
--     (Message Page Field equals 0x555)
-- 25. The GEM should then transmit alternating /C/ codes with the Conf_Reg field incdicating the 
--     same values that are in the PCS next page register plus bit 14 should be set high.
--     This bit tells the link partner that the GEM has successfully received the link next
--     page information. 
--     (Message Page Field equals 0x555)
-- 26. Provide a link of /C/ codes which correspond to the link partner sending a Message Page. 
--     Link partner does have Next Pages to exchange. Furthermore, the link partner
--     acknowledges the reception of the GEMs Next Page information. (Enter COMPLETE_ACKNOWLEDGE)
--     (Message Page Field equals 0x555)
-- 27. Once the GEM enters COMPLETE_ACKNOWLEGE state, the GEM will trigger the PCS next page request interrupt.
--     Then, load the PCS auto-nego. next page register with the desired value. Bit 15 should be set
--     in the PCS Auto-Neg. Next Page register to tell the link partner it has next pages to exchange.
-- 28. The GEM should transmit the contents of the PCS Auto-Negotiation Next Page Register. 
--     Note that the Link Partner has its NP bit set in it's base page advertisment register
--     to allow the exchange of Next Pages with the GEM. (Enter NEXT_PAGE_WAIT state)
--     Note: Since the link partner is tranmsitting its next page information before the GEM, the GEM
--           will quickly go into the NEXT_PAGE_WAIT state. Then, proceed immediately into the 
--           ACKNOWLEDGE_DETECT STATE.  Therefore, the GEM will immediately start transmitting its
--           next page information with the acknowledge bit set.
--     (Message Page Field equals 0x7ff)
-- 29. Provide a link of /C/ codes which correspond to the link partner sending a Unformatted Page. 
--     (Enter ACKNOWLEDGE_DETECT state)
--     (Message Page Field equals 0x7ff)
-- 30. The GEM should then transmit alternating /C/ codes with the Conf_Reg field indicating the 
--     same values that are in the PCS next page register plus bit 14 should be set high.
--     This bit tells the link partner that the GEM has successfully received the link partner next
--     page information. 
--     (Message Page Field equals 0x7ff)
-- 31. Provide a link of /C/ codes which correspond to the link partner sending a Unformatted Page. 
--     The link partner acknowledges the reception of the GEMs Next Page information. 
--     (Enter COMPLETE_ACKNOWLEDGE state)
--     (Message Page Field equals 0x7ff)
-- 32. Once the GEM enters COMPLETE_ACKNOWLEGE state, the GEM will trigger the PCS next page request interrupt.
--     Then, load the PCS auto-nego. next page register with the desired value. Bit 15 should be set
--     in the PCS Auto-Neg. Next Page register to tell the link partner it has next pages to exchange.
-- 33. The GEM should transmit the contents of the PCS Auto-Negotiation Next Page Register. 
--     Note that the Link Partner has its NP bit set in it's base page advertisment register
--     to allow the exchange of Next Pages with the GEM. (Enter NEXT_PAGE_WAIT state)
--     Note: Since the link partner is tranmsitting its next page information before the GEM, the GEM
--           will quickly go into the NEXT_PAGE_WAIT state. Then, proceed immediately into the 
--           ACKNOWLEDGE_DETECT STATE.  Therefore, the GEM will immediately start transmitting its
--           next page information with the acknowledge bit set.
--     (Message Page Field equals 0x555)
-- 34. Provide a link of /C/ codes which correspond to the link partner sending a Unformatted Page. 
--     Link partner does have Next Pages to exchange. (Enter ACKNOWLEDGE_DETECT state)
--     (Message Page Field equals 0x7ff)
-- 35. The GEM should then transmit alternating /C/ codes with the Conf_Reg field incdicating the 
--     same values that are in the PCS next page register plus bit 14 should be set high.
--     This bit tells the link partner that the GEM has successfully received the link next
--     page information. 
--     (Message Page Field equals 0x7ff)
-- 36. Provide a link of /C/ codes which correspond to the link partner sending a Unformatted Page. 
--     Link partner does have Next Pages to exchange. Furthermore, the link partner
--     acknowledges the reception of the GEMs Next Page information. (Enter COMPLETE_ACKNOWLEDGE)
--     (Message Page Field equals 0x7ff)
-- 37. Once the GEM enters COMPLETE_ACKNOWLEGE state, the GEM will trigger the PCS next page request interrupt.
--     No more next page information to exchange. Just check pcs registers.

pinsc(50) loopback 0 half_duplex 1  extint 0 speed 0 --  check reset state

